    "published_method": {
      "cohort": "Longitudinal case with bilateral Ilizarov arm lengthening of approximately 10 cm. The PPS result reports case pre/post assessments and one comparison row. Control counts differ across the publication.",
      "sound": "Two fixed loudspeakers, near at 5 cm from hand and far separated 25 or 100 cm from near. White-noise bursts last 150 ms and are matched to 70 dB at the ear.",
      "timing": "Near audio onset is simultaneous with touch. Far audio leads touch by 5 ms at emission. Actual acoustic arrival time is unverified.",
      "touch": "Two DS7A units on dorsal right index, individually titrated weak target (approximately 90% detected) and strong non-target (100%).",
